{
  "_id": "job17",
  "book": {
    "_id": "job",
    "title": "Job",
    "titleShort": "Job",
    "titleOfficial": "",
    "subtitle": "",
    "summary": "",
    "chapterDelineation": "Chapter"
  },
  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Job",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 17,
    "summary": "Job speaks of the sorrow of death and of the grave in that day when the body returns to the dust.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "My breath is corrupt, my days are extinct, the graves are ready for me.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 3,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "HEB spirit is consumed."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 63
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Are there not mockers with me? and doth not mine eye continue in their provocation?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 9
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Lay down now, put me in a surety with thee; who is he that will strike hands with me?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 12,
            "text": "IE Lay down a pledge."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 48,
            "end": 50
          },
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 58
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For thou hast hid their heart from understanding: therefore shalt thou not exalt them.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 81,
            "end": 86
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that speaketh flattery to his friends, even the eyes of his children shall fail.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 25,
            "text": "TG Flatter."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 32
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He hath made me also a byword of the people; and aforetime I was as a tabret.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 58,
            "text": "HEB I am as an abomination before men."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Mine eye also is dim by reason of sorrow, and all my members are as a shadow.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 61,
            "end": 64
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Upright men shall be astonied at this, and the innocent shall stir up himself against the hypocrite.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 11
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The righteous also shall hold on his way, and he that hath clean hands shall be stronger and stronger.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 70,
            "text": "2 Ne. 25:16; D&C 88:86."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But as for you all, do ye return, and come now: for I cannot find one wise man among you.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 69
          },
          {
            "start": 75,
            "end": 78
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "My days are past, my purposes are broken off, even the thoughts of my heart.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 3,
            "end": 7,
            "text": "Job 7:6."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 50
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "They change the night into day: the light is short because of darkness.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 44
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "If I wait, the grave is mine house: I have made my bed in the darkness.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 34,
            "text": "Eccl. 12:5; Alma 40:11."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 23
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "I have said to corruption, Thou art my father: to the worm, Thou art my mother, and my sister.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 35
          },
          {
            "start": 60,
            "end": 68
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And where is now my hope? as for my hope, who shall see it?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 12
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "They shall go down to the bars of the pit, when our rest together is in the dust.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 48,
            "end": 51
          },
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 68
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
  "nextChapterId": "job18",
  "prevChapterId": "job16",
  "volume": {
    "_id": "oldtestament",
    "title": "Old Testament",
    "titleShort": "OT",
    "titleOfficial": "The Old Testament"
  }
}